  "sourceHtml": "<p>This is a significant release of <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\">Datasette Agent</a>. The most notable new feature is called the <strong>panel</strong> - it lets the agent chat open and then sit next to pages from Datasette, for example a table or query page.</p><p>When combined with <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-apps\">datasette-apps</a> this means you can prompt a database-backed app into existence and then modify it from the chat that sits next to that app.</p><p><img alt=\"Screenshot of a split-screen chat interface titled &quot;evaluate llm prices&quot; (model tag &quot;gpt-6-luna&quot;): the conversation runs in a narrow column on the left, and a wide side panel on the right displays the app the assistant built, with &quot;EXPORT&quot; and &quot;Close panel&quot; buttons above it. In the chat, blue user bubbles read &quot;Build an app to help explore this data&quot; and &quot;give it a more hacker aesthetic design&quot;, each followed by collapsed tool calls (app_create, app_render, app_view, app_str_replace), &quot;LLM Price Explorer v1.&quot; and &quot;v2.&quot; entries with &quot;View app&quot; and &quot;Edit&quot; buttons, and short assistant replies describing the app and its new dark terminal-inspired theme. The right panel shows the resulting &quot;LLM Price Explorer&quot; in neon green monospace on black: stat cards for 185 models from 12 providers with workload costs from $0.042 (Jev 1.13) to $300.00 (o1 Pro), filter and workload cost estimate controls, and a table of matching models with input, output and cached input prices per million tokens.\" src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/datasette-agent-panel.webp\"></p><p>You can try it by signing in with your GitHub account to <a href=\"https://agent.datasette.io/\">agent.datasette.io</a>.</p>",
  "sourceHash": "df35a19696fd11216074093737efb3bf5a4d159de19c300b29726b8bc670063f",
  "language": "und",
